.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle build"
creates two kinds of output.
An image is made from a source file and requires only the Wattle
runtime.
Executables,
native libraries and WebAssembly programs are made from the
artifacts that a Wattle project declares in its info file and
require the Zig toolchain.
.Pp
.Nm "wattle build"
can be invoked using
.Cm wattle b .
.
.Ss Subcommands
An image is made from a source file,
not from a project’s info file,
and requires nothing further.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Cm img
.Xc
Loads the module at
.Ar source
and writes an image of its environment to
.Ar output .
If
.Ar output
is omitted,
it is
.Ar source
with
.Ql "\&.wattle"
replaced by
.Ql "\&.wimage" .
.Xr wattle-run 1
can be used to load the image later.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-lib"
.Ar module
.Xc
Imports
.Ar module
into the environment before
.Ar source
is loaded,
as
.Ic "wattle run"
does.
Several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.El
.El
.Pp
Executables,
native libraries and web programs are made from the artifacts
declared in the project’s info file and require the Zig toolchain.
The generated files are in
.Ql "zig-out"
in the project root.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm exe
.Xc
Builds the artifacts of
