.Ss Zig toolchain
Building executables,
native libraries and web programs requires:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Cm zig
to be on the user’s
.Ev PATH .
.It
The Wattle source,
which is included in Wattle releases and which is installed
to
.Ql "<prefix>/share/wattle" .
.El
.Pp
No Zig build files are required.
.Nm "wattle build"
creates temporary
.Ql "build\&.zig"
and
.Ql "build\&.zig\&.zon"
files using the description of the artifacts in the project’s
info file.
It then uses these to build with
.Cm zig .
.Pp
The project’s info file is
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory.
.
.Ss Declarations
A project author declares the artifacts in the project’s info
file in a vector under the
.Ql ":artifacts"
key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :artifacts \(lB{:type :lib
              :name \(dqgreet\(dq
              :root \(dqgreet\&.zig\(dq}
             {:type :exe
              :name \(dqhello\(dq
              :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq
              :libs \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.Pp
Every artifact has:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
a
.Ql ":type"
(\c
.Ql ":exe" ,
.Ql ":lib" ,
.Ql ":web"
or
.Ql ":src" )
.It
a
.Ql ":name"
(a unique string of letters,
digits,
.Ql "_"
and
.Ql "-" )
.El
.Pp
Artifacts of the following types have additional requirements:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":exe"
.Xc
This requires an
.Ql ":entry"
key that maps to the file where
.Ql "main"
is defined.
It may also include a
.Ql ":libs"
key that maps to a vector of native library artifacts that will
be linked into it.
.It Xo
.Ql ":lib"
.Xc
This requires a
.Ql ":root"
key that maps to the Zig root file of a native module.
.It Xo
.Ql ":web"
.Xc
This requires an
.Ql ":entry"
key that maps to the file where
.Ql "main"
is defined.
.It Xo
.Ql ":src"
.Xc
A program that
.Ql "wattle apps install"
installs as source.
.Ql "wattle build"
does not build it.
This requires an
.Ql ":entry"
key that maps to the file where
.Ql "main"
is defined and a
.Ql ":files"
key that maps to a vector of the paths to install.
It may also include a
.Ql ":libs"
key that maps to a vector of native library artifacts that are
built when it is installed.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.El
.
.Ss Web programs
Web programs are artifacts that are designed to run in a browser
environment.
To do this,
.Nm "wattle build"
.Cm web
creates four files in
.Ql "zig-out/web/<name>/" :
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "wattle-<hash>\&.wasm" ,
the runtime
.It
.Ql "<name>-<hash>\&.wimage" ,
the program
.It
.Ql "wasi-<hash>\&.js" ,
the WASI support shim
.It
.Ql "<name>\&.js" ,
an ES module that exports
.Ql "load"
and
.Ql "run"
.El
.Pp
Example programs are distributed with the Wattle source tree.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compile a program into an image and run the image:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle build img hello\&.wattle hello\&.wimage
$ wattle run -i hello\&.wimage Alice
.Ed
.Pp
Build the executables that the project’s info file declares,
optimised for size:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle -p /usr/local build exe --release small
.Ed
.
